# Part 7
c(135, "Part 7 — the review-prompt problem: 8 direct complaints ('Why won't it progress without me writing a review?'; 'in the middle of the onboarding questions the app interrupts me to ask me to rate'); indirect evidence table (verbatim): ≤25-char reviews 7.2% → 13.8% → 33.4%, median body 156 → 107 → 53 chars; substantive mean 3.83 → 3.51 → 3.10", "tactic",
  "Tactic and outcome: an in-app review prompt fired during onboarding — 8 direct complaints ('Me pide evaluar la app sin haberla usado'; 'Why won't it progress without me writing a review?'; 'in the middle of the onboarding questions the app interrupts me to ask me to rate and review') — and much larger indirect evidence: ≤25-character reviews 7.2% → 13.8% → 33.4% (150 of 196 5★ in E3), median body length 156 → 107 → 53 characters, 'haven't used it yet' 3.0% → 2.9% → 3.8%; all-records mean 3.87 → 3.66 → 3.60 vs substantive 3.83 → 3.51 → 3.10; a 4★ from Australia says the app would not let them proceed without writing a review — if that gate existed in any build, the 5★ share is not a satisfaction measurement for that period",
  "onboarding review prompt, possibly gating progress", "5★-burst", table("**Indirect evidence, which is much larger:**") + " ; 8 direct (0.61%, mean 2.00)", "dont", "very strong", "yes",
  ["12424719394","12591004629","12957806563","13411399713","13419192067","13386578145","13764701322","12876930985"])
